{
  "tema": 6076,
  "slug": "esperar-que-subjuntivo",
  "titulo": "Using esperar que + present subjunctive to express hope",
  "subtitulo": "Espero que vengas: hope about someone else takes the subjunctive.",
  "foto": "t09.jpg",
  "regla": "Esperar que + present subjunctive expresses hope about something that happens or will happen. Same subject: esperar + infinitive.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To say you **hope** something happens or will happen, use **esperar que** + the **present subjunctive**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "**esperar**",
            "**que**",
            "present subjunctive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "English often uses the future here (_I hope you'll come_), but Spanish uses the present subjunctive: **espero que vengas**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Using the ordinary present after **esperar que** is wrong: **espero que sales** ✗ → **espero que salgas**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The subjunctive is used only when the two subjects are **different**. When it's the **same** subject, drop **que** and use the **infinitive**: **espero viajar**, not **espero que yo viaje**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: same pattern as [[5059|querer que]]: two people, **que** and subjunctive; one person, infinitive."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Espero que ==vengas== hoy en la noche.",
              "en": "I hope you'll come tonight."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi hermano y yo esperamos que ==tengas== mucha suerte con la chamba.",
              "en": "My brother and I hope you have lots of luck with the job."
            },
            {
              "es": "Espero que ==sean== muy felices.",
              "en": "I hope they'll be very happy."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los jefes esperan que ==entiendan== la situación.",
              "en": "The bosses hope you all understand the situation."
            },
            {
              "es": "Espero que ==salgas== conmigo al cine.",
              "en": "I hope you'll come to the movies with me."
            },
            {
              "es": "Espero ==viajar== a Japón algún día.",
              "en": "I hope to travel to Japan someday. (same subject)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Espero que sales conmigo."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Espero que salgas conmigo."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Never the ordinary present."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Espero que vendrás."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Espero que vengas."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Not the future either."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Espero que yo viaje a Japón."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Espero viajar a Japón."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Same subject: infinitive."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
